    {
      "id": "03-two-way-swap-despite-both-seats-occupied",
      "why": "Both target seats are occupied when the batch starts: the same address is an active member in t-a and in t-b. Each move sends one of them to the other tenant, so each move's target is currently held by the other move's source. Occupancy is judged after every source has left, so the swap succeeds; a per-move check would wrongly refuse it.",
      "start_at": "2026-01-01T00:00:00Z",
